WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.320
FedRAMP emphasizes continuous monitoring rather than one-time assessment.

2
00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:15.535
Cloud environments change, vulnerabilities appear, configurations evolve, users change, incidents occur, and services continue to develop after authorization.

3
00:00:15.535 --> 00:00:27.957
Continuous monitoring helps organizations maintain visibility into security controls, vulnerabilities, system changes, operational risks, and remediation activities over time.

4
00:00:27.957 --> 00:00:40.439
Monitoring may include vulnerability scanning, configuration management, incident reporting, plan of action updates, control status reporting, change tracking, and review of security-relevant events.

5
00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:43.981
The goal is not to collect information for its own sake.

6
00:00:43.981 --> 00:00:53.400
Monitoring should help agencies, providers, and stakeholders understand whether the cloud service continues to operate within an acceptable risk posture.

7
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.633
Continuous monitoring also supports accountability.

8
00:00:56.633 --> 00:01:06.002
If a control weakens, a vulnerability remains open, or a system change affects the security boundary, decision makers need current information.

9
00:01:06.002 --> 00:01:11.480
For technical teams, continuous monitoring connects FedRAMP to daily operations.

10
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:22.076
Patch management, logging, alerting, change control, vulnerability remediation, incident response, and configuration review all contribute to the security picture.

11
00:01:22.076 --> 00:01:25.169
The practical takeaway is that FedRAMP is ongoing.

12
00:01:25.169 --> 00:01:32.304
Authorization is not the end of the work; it is part of a lifecycle that depends on sustained visibility and management.

13
00:01:32.304 --> 00:01:36.714
Continuous monitoring also supports better conversations with agencies.

14
00:01:36.714 --> 00:01:47.021
Current information about vulnerabilities, changes, incidents, and remediation gives stakeholders a clearer view of whether the service remains within expected risk boundaries.

15
00:01:47.021 --> 00:01:51.950
For program teams, this means monitoring evidence should be reliable and repeatable.

16
00:01:51.950 --> 00:02:00.072
The organization needs processes that can produce current information without rebuilding the entire security story from scratch each month.
